iting",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"K.W.6","","standard","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"K.W.6.1","","expectation","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"K.W.7","","standard","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"K.W.7.1","","expectation","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"K.W.8","","standard","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"K.W.8.1","","expectation","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[1,"128.2(b)(1)(A)","listen actively and ask questions to understand information and answer questions using multi-word responses;","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.2(b)(1)(B)","restate and follow oral directions that involve a short, related sequence of actions;","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.2(b)(1)(C)","share information and ideas by speaking audibly and clearly using the conventions of language;","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.2(b)(1)(D)","work collaboratively with others by following agreed-upon rules for discussion, including taking turns; and","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.2(b)(1)(E)","develop social communication such as introducing himself/herself, using common greetings, and expressing needs and wants.","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.2(b)(2)(A)","demonstrate phonological awareness by: (i) identifying and producing rhyming words; (ii) recognizing spoken alliteration or groups of words that begin with the same simple syllable or initial sound; (iii) identifying the individual words in a spoken sentence; (iv) identifying syllables in spoken words; (v) blending syllables to form multisyllabic words; (vi) segmenting multisyllabic words into syllables; (vii) identifying initial and final sounds in simple words; (viii) blending spoken phonemes to form syllables; and (ix) manipulating syllables within a multisyllabic word;","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.2(b)(2)(B)","demonstrate and apply phonetic knowledge by: (i) identifying and matching the common sounds that letters represent; (ii) using letter-sound relationships to decode one- and two-syllable words and multisyllabic words, including CV, VC, CCV, CVC, VCV, CVCV, CCVCV, and CVCCV; (iii) decoding words with silent h and consonant digraphs such as/ch/,/rr/, and/ll/; and (iv) recognizing that new words are created when syllables are changed, added, or deleted;","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.2(b)(2)(C)","demonstrate and apply spelling knowledge by: (i) spelling common letter and sound correlations; and (ii) spelling words with common syllabic patterns such as CV, VC, CCV, CVC, VCV, CVCV, CCVCV, and CVCCV;","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.2(b)(2)(D)","demonstrate print awareness by: (i) identifying the front cover, back cover, and title page of a book; (ii) holding a book right side up, turning pages correctly, and knowing that reading moves from top to bottom and left to right with return sweep; (iii) recognizing that sentences are comprised of words separated by spaces and recognizing word boundaries; (iv) recognizing the difference between a letter and a printed word; and (v) identifying all uppercase and lowercase letters; and","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.2(b)(2)(E)","develop handwriting by accurately forming all uppercase and lowercase letters using appropriate directionality.","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.2(b)(3)(A)","use a resource such as a picture dictionary or digital resource to find words;","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.2(b)(3)(B)","use illustrations and texts the student is able to read or hear to learn or clarify word meanings; and","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.2(b)(3)(C)","identify and use words that name actions; directions; positions; sequences; categories such as colors, shapes, and textures; and locations.","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.2(b)(4)","Developing and sustaining foundational language skills: listening, speaking, reading, writing, and thinking--self-sustained reading. The student reads grade-appropriate texts independently. The student is expected to self-select text and interact independently with text for increasing periods of time.","strand","4",null],[1,"128.2(b)(5)(A)","establish purpose for reading assigned and self-selected texts with adult assistance;","expectation","5",null],[1,"128.2(b)(5)(B)","generate questions about text before, during, and after reading to deepen understanding and gain information with adult assistance;","expectation","5",null],[1,"128.2(b)(5)(C)","make and confirm predictions using text features and structures with adult assistance;","expectation","5",null],[1,"128.2(b)(5)(D)","create mental images to deepen understanding with adult assistance;","expectation","5",null],[1,"128.2(b)(5)(E)","make connections to personal experiences, ideas in other texts, and society with adult assistance;","expectation","5",null],[1,"128.2(b)(5)(F)","make inferences and use evidence to support understanding with adult assistance;","expectation","5",null],[1,"128.2(b)(5)(G)","evaluate details to determine what is most important with adult assistance;","expectation","5",null],[1,"128.2(b)(5)(H)","synthesize information to create new understanding with adult assistance; and","expectation","5",null],[1,"128.2(b)(5)(I)","monitor comprehension and make adjustments such as re-reading, using background knowledge, checking for visual cues, and asking questions when understanding breaks down with adult assistance.","expectation","5",null],[1,"128.2(b)(6)(A)","describe personal connections to a variety of sources;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.2(b)(6)(B)","provide an oral, pictorial, or written response to a text;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.2(b)(6)(C)","use text evidence to support an appropriate response;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.2(b)(6)(D)","retell texts in ways that maintain meaning;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.2(b)(6)(E)","interact with sources in meaningful ways such as illustrating or writing; and","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.2(b)(6)(F)","respond using newly acquired vocabulary as appropriate.","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.2(b)(7)(A)","discuss topics and determine the basic theme using text evidence with adult assistance;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.2(b)(7)(B)","identify and describe the main character(s);","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.2(b)(7)(C)","describe the elements of plot development, including the main events, the problem, and the resolution, for texts read aloud with adult assistance; and","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.2(b)(7)(D)","describe the setting.","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.2(b)(8)(A)","demonstrate knowledge of distinguishing characteristics of well-known children's literature such as folktales, fables, fairy tales, and nursery rhymes;","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.2(b)(8)(B)","discuss rhyme and rhythm in nursery rhymes and a variety of poems;","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.2(b)(8)(C)","discuss main characters in drama;","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.2(b)(8)(D)","recognize characteristics and structures of informational text, including: (i) the central idea and supporting evidence with adult assistance; (ii) titles and simple graphics to gain information; and (iii) the steps in a sequence with adult assistance;","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.2(b)(8)(E)","recognize characteristics of persuasive text with adult assistance and state what the author is trying to persuade the reader to think or do; and","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.2(b)(8)(F)","recognize characteristics of multimodal and digital texts.","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.2(b)(9)(A)","discuss with adult assistance the author's purpose for writing texts;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.2(b)(9)(B)","discuss with adult assistance how the use of text structure contributes to the author's purpose;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.2(b)(9)(C)","discuss with adult assistance the author's use of print and graphic features to achieve specific purposes;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.2(b)(9)(D)","discuss with adult assistance how the author uses words that help the reader visualize; and","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.2(b)(9)(E)","listen to and experience first- and third-person texts.","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.2(b)(10)(A)","plan by generating ideas for writing through class discussions and drawings;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.2(b)(10)(B)","develop drafts in oral, pictorial, or written form by organizing ideas;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.2(b)(10)(C)","revise drafts by adding details in pictures or words;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.2(b)(10)(D)","edit drafts with adult assistance using standard Spanish conventions, including: (i) complete sentences; (ii) verbs, including the difference between ser and estar; (iii) singular and plural nouns, including gender-specific articles; (iv) adjectives, including articles; (v) prepositions; (vi) pronouns, including personal, and the difference in the use of formal pronoun usted and informal pronoun tú; (vii) capitalization of the first letter in a sentence and names; (viii) punctuation marks at the end of declarative sentences; and (ix) correct spelling of words with grade-appropriate orthographic patterns and rules; and","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.2(b)(10)(E)","share writing.","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.2(b)(11)(A)","dictate or compose literary texts, including personal narratives; and","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.2(b)(11)(B)","dictate or compose informational texts.","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.2(b)(12)(A)","generate questions for formal and informal inquiry with adult assistance;","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.2(b)(12)(B)","develop and follow a research plan with adult assistance;","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.2(b)(12)(C)","gather information from a variety of sources with adult assistance;","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.2(b)(12)(D)","demonstrate understanding of information gathered with adult assistance; and","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.2(b)(12)(E)","use an appropriate mode of delivery, whether written, oral, or multimodal, to present results.","expectation","12",null]]}